Date: Wed, 30 Nov 2022 18:46:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] winex11: Support fixed X11 keycode to scancode
 conversion.

X11 keycodes are just Linux keycodes + 8 nowadays according to evdev or
libinput drivers, and we can avoid innacurate reconstruction in the most
common case.

Wine-Bug: https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=30984
Wine-Bug: https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=45605

Upstreamed in wine-mirror 11.20 in a different shape: keyc2scan() is now a
function which maps base keys directly (keycode - 8, KEY_KPDOT range plus
evdev KEY_* cases) and init_default_keyc2scan() fills the non-XKB fallback
table. The keyboard_scancode_detect toggle this patch added has no
counterpart upstream. Only a note remains so the series step still
validates; the winecfg toggle UI from 6/9 remains but currently wires to no
backend.
---
 dlls/winex11.drv/keyboard.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/keyboard.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/keyboard.c
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/keyboard.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/keyboard.c
@@ -147,4 +147,5 @@ static WORD keyc2scan( unsigned int keycode, unsigned int state )

     /* base keys can be mapped directly */
     if (key <= KEY_KPDOT) return key;
+    /* GE-Proton scancodes 8/9: upstreamed (fixed keycode - 8 mapping). */

 #ifdef KEY_SYSRQ
     /* map keys found in KBDTABLES definitions (Txx Xxx Yxx macros) */
